{"title":"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Vieta&#39;s_Formulas)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Vieta's Formulas)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Inequality_Logic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Inequality Logic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A parabola has vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7622d385697455ceedc5591de0949ee9b878b8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,-5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> and has two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31572a833f4041c91695248e85c6f3a17ed948fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />intercepts, one positive, and one negative. If this parabola is the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f587d3ffdf44a0c19b0a815c6244eef505bfbc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ax^2 + bx + c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" /> which of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/3494a9fb574982968c51cf1f94b82f5b1538e31c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\text{only}\\ a \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\text{only}\\ b \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\text{only}\\ c \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } a\\ \\text{and}\\ b\\ \\text{only} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\text{none}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"557\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Vieta.27s_Formulas.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Vieta's_Formulas)\">Solution 1 (Vieta's Formulas)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Vieta&#39;s Formulas)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The vertex of the parabola is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7622d385697455ceedc5591de0949ee9b878b8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,-5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />.  Since there are two x-intercepts, it must open upwards.  If it opened downard, there would be no roots.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The x-coordinate of the vertex is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b250a7d94be19932d73b6f79e32ec07dbb15e390.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"37\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, and the x-intercept is positive, the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa30e2beb1820f6b39f6251023709c8165cefc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> must be positive too, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is negative.\n</p><p>By Vieta, the product of the two roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84719dcd9659dc2554a5e6701617224a5af26b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" />.  Since the two roots are a positive number and a negative number, the product is negative.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be negative.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" /> is the right answer - only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is positive.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Inequality_Logic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Inequality_Logic)\">Solution 2 (Inequality Logic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Inequality Logic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The vertex is given to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b9130590890a02e2409df6db0bd4d46ab69b2bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, -5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. This means the equation can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a16ad7526544864e850c13a3e4bfadca0921a5cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = a(x - 4)^2 - 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Since there are 2 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercepts, the parabola must open up and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Expanding the vertex form gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb230dc0c24a337c30b2ee540dc53f4f40b997e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = a(x^2 - 8x + 16) - 5\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed710e08f827f0522633db46975e28543fb34f81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = ax^2 - 8ax + 16a - 5\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d1280aaaae30b2baf0e2e58db4d846fc56a90634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = -8a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da91e1e72551cbbd740d728ec916ee490883d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 16a - 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, we must have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e9d5f645951ecd3b8d0f8e3fd18346dcd1fe3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-8a &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" /> and thus that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beab3b5c143f2b58c18e15cdb470a15386701dab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>To determine the sign of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercepts by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c664d925cc23f904286742fa535bb560be5466.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a(x - 4)^2 - 5 = 0\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e783a5dbc18a77dacc887102d6b403a38c02fc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a(x - 4)^2 = 5\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/06984d3dc3a0c2469f9ec021161ac827f32e938c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x - 4)^2 = \\frac{5}{a}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f070dcf9c2d4c7ec221e23f8397187db0e5323.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 4 \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{a}}\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The problem states there is exactly one negative root. This means the smaller of the two roots must be less than zero:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83cd9d670b75546380bbf5e9fc320e4d64e4bc5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 - \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{a}} &lt; 0\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2ee9be770f59e480ddfa144f4e7b98b3e7d4d6a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4 &lt; \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{a}}\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Since both sides are strictly positive, we can square the inequality:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17bde4c55f83be02076a03040e3ce386d883ec7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16 &lt; \\frac{5}{a}\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, we can multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> without changing the direction of the inequality sign:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb61c7007c9c1488cab73af0de1d4f8e354970e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16a &lt; 5\\]\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815fe9058e85c9cb9cfa11fafe88d188b4a93bd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16a - 5 &lt; 0\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since our expansion gave that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da91e1e72551cbbd740d728ec916ee490883d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 16a - 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />, this shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3dd417591a694e2339db5d9c3666343ee396e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f8e89641a5b0ca6dec91e8d1e1c0fe9d4f05a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{only } a \\text{ is positive}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"137\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME\" title=\"1998 AHSME\">1998 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 296/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8073/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.692      1 -total\n 58.12%    7.376      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 39.59%    5.025      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9490:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190945 and revision id 288990. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}